  "relation_to_original_evidence": {
    "source_center_census": "Original block-029 evidence shows 633 center rows contact only six VCT family features. This new whole-source-polygon comparison tests only the three named regional candidate families and is not a global candidate-family census.",
    "physical_receipt": "One actual stock physical run was completed previously for the six target features; 4 rows had no flagged issue, Saint George had extra_reconstruction, Grenadines had missing_reconstruction plus extra_reconstruction. These adverse issues remain even though none intersects the 633 original cell intervals in the prior native key comparison.",
    "authority_source_membership": "Official regional references establish a plausible geographic competitor screen and the retained source products bound their own archived geometries. They do not establish current government adoption, legal jurisdiction, source applicability, maritime claims, or whether the 2017 VCT representation is correct/current."
  },
  "remaining_limits": [
    "The official SVG source describes Grenadines islands, Saint Lucia, and Barbados geographically, not administrative or maritime sovereignty boundaries. This analysis makes no territorial or legal inference.",
    "The result does not eliminate other global, out-of-date, unsupplied, or unnamed sources; nor does it prove the original contract’s full relevant competitor set has been exhaustively enumerated.",
    "The near Grenada-VCT source gap is material to source applicability; exact current official treatment of Grenadine islands remains unverified.",
    "The physical receipt has adverse sub-cell flags for Saint George and Grenadines; zero original-cell-key intersection does not erase whole-target adverse findings.",
    "No positive repair qualification or root acceptance is asserted. The distinct 389-cell/179-interval companion remains excluded. ODbL, CC BY-SA, CC0 and CC BY metadata are preserved as recorded terms only; no legal clearance conclusion."
  ],
